<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
    <head>
        <%
        const faqExportValues = (Array.isArray(exportFormats) ? exportFormats : [])
            .map((format) => String(format?.value || '').trim().toLowerCase())
            .filter(Boolean);
        const faqLegacyExportsEnabled = faqExportValues.some((value) => value !== 'ltd');
        const pageTitle = 'Nintendo Mii Characters FAQ - Formats, LTD & Conversion';
        const pageDesc = 'Answers about Mii characters, transfers, QR codes, file formats, LTD conversion, and the limits of LTD previews on InfiniMii.';
        const canonicalUrl = `${baseUrl}/faq`;
        const keywords = 'mii faq, mii questions, what is a mii, mii help, mii guide, nintendo mii, tomodachi life, mii maker';
        const breadcrumbs = [
            { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
            { name: 'FAQ', url: '/faq' }
        ];
        const schemaType = 'FAQPage';
        const schemaGraphs = [{
            "@context": "https://schema.org",
            "@type": "FAQPage",
            "mainEntity": [
                {
                    "@type": "Question",
                    "name": "What is a Mii character?",
                    "acceptedAnswer": {
                        "@type": "Answer",
                        "text": "A Mii is a customizable Nintendo avatar used across systems like Wii, 3DS, Wii U, and Switch."
                    }
                },
                {
                    "@type": "Question",
                    "name": "How do I transfer Miis between Nintendo systems?",
                    "acceptedAnswer": {
                        "@type": "Answer",
                        "text": "Transfer methods depend on the systems involved and can include QR codes, Amiibo, direct system tools, file conversion, or manual recreation."
                    }
                },
                {
                    "@type": "Question",
                    "name": "What is a Mii QR code?",
                    "acceptedAnswer": {
                        "@type": "Answer",
                        "text": "A Mii QR code stores Mii data in a scannable image that compatible Nintendo systems can import."
                    }
                },
                {
                    "@type": "Question",
                    "name": faqLegacyExportsEnabled ? 'Can I convert Miis between Nintendo systems?' : 'Can I convert older Mii files to LTD?',
                    "acceptedAnswer": {
                        "@type": "Answer",
                        "text": faqLegacyExportsEnabled
                            ? 'InfiniMii accepts supported Mii files and converts them to the formats listed in its export tools.'
                            : 'Miis from Living the Dream keep their original LTD files. Miis from other systems can use the compatible export formats listed on the site.'
                    }
                },
                {
                    "@type": "Question",
                    "name": "What are official Miis?",
                    "acceptedAnswer": {
                        "@type": "Answer",
                        "text": "Official Miis are Miis that appeared in Nintendo games, promotions, system software, or other verified official materials."
                    }
                }
            ]
        }];
        %>
        <%- include('metaTags', { title: pageTitle, description: pageDesc, canonicalUrl, keywords }) %>
        <%- include('structuredData') %>
        <link rel="stylesheet" href="/global.css">
        <link rel="stylesheet" href="/utilityPages.css">
    </head>
    <body>
        <%- include('globalStyle') %>
        <%- include('header') %>
        <%- include('accountDisplay') %>
        
        <main class="content faq-content" role="main">
            <%- include('sidebar') %>
            
            <article class="faq-article">
                <h1>Mii Characters: Frequently Asked Questions</h1>
                <p class="faq-lede">A practical guide to what Miis are, how transfers work, and which tools to use when you want to move or share them.</p>
                
                <nav class="faq-nav" aria-label="FAQ Categories">
                    <h2>Browse by topic</h2>
                    <ul class="faq-nav-list">
                        <li><a href="#basics">Mii Basics</a></li>
                        <li><a href="#transfer">Transferring Miis</a></li>
                        <li><a href="#qr-codes">QR Codes</a></li>
                        <li><a href="#ltd-support">LTD Support</a></li>
                        <li><a href="#systems">Nintendo Systems</a></li>
                        <li><a href="#infinimii">Using InfiniMii</a></li>
                    </ul>
                </nav>
                
                <!-- Mii Basics Section -->
                <section id="basics" class="faq-section">
                    <h2>Mii Basics</h2>
                    
                    <div class="faq-item" itemscope itemprop="mainEntity" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question">
                        <h3 itemprop="name">What is a Mii character?</h3>
                        <div itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
                            <div itemprop="text">
                                <p><strong>A Mii</strong> is a digital avatar character created and used on <strong>Nintendo gaming systems</strong> including the Wii, Nintendo DS, Nintendo 3DS, Wii U, and Nintendo Switch.</p>
                                <p>You can create a Mii based on yourself, another person, or a fictional character. Editable details include:</p>
                                <ul>
                                    <li>Adjustable facial features (eyes, nose, mouth)</li>
                                    <li>Various hairstyles and colors</li>
                                    <li>Accessories (glasses, facial hair, hats)</li>
                                    <li>Body size and proportions</li>
                                    <li>Favorite colors</li>
                                </ul>
                                <p>They appear in games, system menus, and social features across Nintendo platforms.</p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    
                    <div class="faq-item" itemscope itemprop="mainEntity" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question">
                        <h3 itemprop="name">What Nintendo systems use Mii characters?</h3>
                        <div itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
                            <div itemprop="text">
                                <p>Mii characters are used on:</p>
                                <ul>
                                    <li><strong>Nintendo Wii</strong> (2006) - Original Mii system with Mii Channel</li>
                                    <li><strong>Nintendo DS</strong> (limited support in some games)</li>
                                    <li><strong>Nintendo 3DS</strong> (2011) - Enhanced with QR codes, StreetPass</li>
                                    <li><strong>Wii U</strong> (2012) - Full Mii integration with GamePad</li>
                                    <li><strong>Nintendo Switch</strong> (2017) - Modern Mii system</li>
                                    <li><strong>Tomodachi Life</strong> (3DS game where Miis are central)</li>
                                    <li><strong>Miitomo</strong> (mobile app, discontinued 2018)</li>
                                    <li><strong>Nintendo Switch 2</strong> - Same as Nintendo Switch</li>
                                    <li><strong>Miitopia & Tomodachi Life</strong> - Expanded features and functions on top of the Miis</li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    
                    <div class="faq-item" itemscope itemprop="mainEntity" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question">
                        <h3 itemprop="name">Can I use Miis in games?</h3>
                        <div itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
                            <div itemprop="text">
                                <p>Yes. Many Nintendo games use Miis as playable characters or NPCs:</p>
                                
                                <h4>Wii Games:</h4>
                                <ul>
                                    <li>Wii Sports, Wii Sports Resort</li>
                                    <li>Wii Play, Wii Music</li>
                                    <li>Mario Kart Wii</li>
                                    <li>Super Smash Bros. Brawl</li>
                                </ul>
                                
                                <h4>3DS/Wii U Games:</h4>
                                <ul>
                                    <li>Tomodachi Life (Miis are the main characters)</li>
                                    <li>Miitopia (Miis are the main characters)</li>
                                    <li>Mario Kart 7, Mario Kart 8</li>
                                    <li>Super Smash Bros. for 3DS/Wii U</li>
                                    <li>StreetPass Mii Plaza</li>
                                </ul>
                                
                                <h4>Switch Games:</h4>
                                <ul>
                                    <li>Super Smash Bros. Ultimate</li>
                                    <li>Mario Kart 8 Deluxe</li>
                                    <li>Miitopia</li>
                                    <li>Mario Golf: Super Rush</li>
                                    <li>Tomodachi Life: Living the Dream</li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </section>
                
                <!-- Transfer Section -->
                <section id="transfer" class="faq-section">
                    <h2>Transferring Miis Between Systems</h2>
                    
                    <div class="faq-item" itemscope itemprop="mainEntity" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question">
                        <h3 itemprop="name">How do I transfer Miis between Nintendo systems?</h3>
                        <div itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
                            <div itemprop="text">
                                <p>Transfer methods depend on which systems you're moving between:</p>
                                
                                <table class="transfer-matrix">
                                    <thead>
                                        <tr>
                                            <th>From → To</th>
                                            <th>Best Method</th>
                                            <th>Difficulty</th>
                                        </tr>
                                    </thead>
                                    <tbody>
                                        <tr>
                                            <td>3DS → 3DS/Wii U</td>
                                            <td>QR Code</td>
                                            <td>Easy</td>
                                        </tr>
                                        <tr>
                                            <td>3DS/Wii U → Switch</td>
                                            <td>Amiibo</td>
                                            <td>Moderate</td>
                                        </tr>
                                        <tr>
                                            <td>Wii → 3DS</td>
                                            <td>Mii Channel/Maker Conversion Process</td>
                                            <td>Easy</td>
                                        </tr>
                                        <tr>
                                            <td>Any → Switch</td>
                                            <td>Manual Recreation</td>
                                            <td>Moderate</td>
                                        </tr>
                                    </tbody>
                                </table>
                                
                                <p><a href="/guides/transfer" class="cta-link">→ Read the transfer guide</a></p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    
                    <!-- Add more transfer FAQs -->
                </section>
                
                <!-- QR Codes Section -->
                <section id="qr-codes" class="faq-section">
                    <h2>QR Codes</h2>
                    
                    <div class="faq-item" itemscope itemprop="mainEntity" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question">
                        <h3 itemprop="name">What is a Mii QR code and how do I use it?</h3>
                        <div itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
                            <div itemprop="text">
                                <p>A <strong>Mii QR code</strong> is a scannable image that contains all the data needed to recreate a Mii character on your Nintendo system.</p>
                                
                                <h4>How to scan a Mii QR code:</h4>
                                <ol>
                                    <li>On your <strong>3DS</strong> or <strong>Wii U</strong>, open <strong>Mii Maker</strong></li>
                                    <li>Tap <strong>"QR Code/Image Options"</strong></li>
                                    <li>Select <strong>"Scan QR Code"</strong></li>
                                    <li>Point your camera at the QR code</li>
                                    <li>The Mii will appear - tap <strong>"OK"</strong> to save</li>
                                </ol>
                                
                                <p>QR codes work with: 3DS, Wii U, Tomodachi Life, and Miitomo (discontinued)</p>
                                
                                <p><a href="/qr" class="cta-link">→ Open the QR scanner</a></p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </section>
                
                <section id="ltd-support" class="faq-section">
                    <h2>Tomodachi Life: Living the Dream</h2>
                    
                    <div class="faq-item" itemscope itemprop="mainEntity" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question">
                        <h3 itemprop="name">How does InfiniMii support Living the Dream Miis?</h3>
                        <div itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
                            <div itemprop="text">
                                <p>InfiniMii keeps native LTD files unchanged. Miis created for Living the Dream can only be downloaded as LTD files. Miis from earlier systems keep the compatible conversion options listed on the site.</p>
                                <p>InfiniMii creates transparent previews for LTD Miis that use data its renderer has verified. If a file contains unverified Mii data, the site does not generate an approximate preview.</p>
                                <p>Some Living the Dream data, including clothing, wardrobe items, and Canvas or user-generated content, cannot yet be rendered reliably. That data remains in the original LTD file even when the site cannot display it.</p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </section>
                
                <section class="still-have-questions">
                    <h2>Need more help?</h2>
                    <p>Ask the community or open a related guide:</p>
                    <ul class="support-links">
                        <li><a href="<%= discordInvite %>" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Join Discord</a> - Get help from the community</li>
                        <li><a href="/upload">Upload a Mii</a> - Add a Mii to your account</li>
                        <li><a href="/guides/transfer">Transfer Guide</a> - Instructions by source and destination system</li>
                    </ul>
                </section>
            </article>
            
            <%- include('featuredMiis') %>
        </main>
        
        <%- include('footer') %>
    </body>
</html>
